## AI Task Ownership

Use `docs\ai-tasks\` for durable agent handoffs. Task filenames must start with one of these owner prefixes:

- `CLINE-`: execute in this VS Code Cline chat.
- `CC-`: handoff for Claude Code in the terminal. In Cline, create or update the file, but do not execute it unless the user explicitly reassigns it to Cline.
- `CODEX-`: handoff for Codex. In Cline, create or update the file, but do not execute it unless the user explicitly reassigns it to Cline.

Every task file must include an `Owner:` line matching its filename prefix and a `Project:` line with `D:\PROJECTS\DarkTreeFPS2022\lfhrnhbagc2022`. If owner and filename disagree, or if `Status: needs-owner-review` is present, do not execute the task yet. Ask the user to confirm the owner or update the filename and `Owner:` together.

